LEG V5 -- `transition-mode true`: v2 AND v3 ADVERTISEMENTS TOGETHER       [PASS]
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The guide p.26: "RFC 5798 for VRRPv3 allows a VRRPv3 virtual router to send
  both VRRPv2 and VRRPv3 advertisements ... Transition mode is disabled by
  default and is enabled by issuing the transition-mode true command."
  The same O-37 ordering constraint applies.        [work/s16-transition-u2.log]
    awplus(config-router)# transition-mode true
    % You must disable this session first
  so:                                              [work/s16b-transition-u2.log]
    disable / transition-mode true / enable  ->  `Transition mode: TRUE`

  ON THE WIRE                                 [work/s16c-transition-wire-u2.log]
    awplus# tcpdump -i vlan10 -c 4 -nn -v -e proto 112
    06:10:07.103828 00:00:5e:00:01:0a > 01:00:5e:00:00:12, length 46:
        (ttl 255, proto VRRP (112), length 32)
        10.38.22.34 > 224.0.0.18: **VRRPv3**, Advertisement, vrid 10, prio 150,
        intvl 100cs, length 12, (bad vrrp cksum 1846), addrs: 10.38.22.36
    06:10:07.103854 00:00:5e:00:01:0a > 01:00:5e:00:00:12, length 54:
        (ttl 255, proto VRRP (112), length 40)
        10.38.22.34 > 224.0.0.18: **VRRPv2**, Advertisement, vrid 10, prio 150,
        authtype none, intvl 1s, length 20, addrs: 10.38.22.36
    ... and the same PAIR again at 06:10:08.104189 / .104214
  => with transition mode on, every advertisement period emits BOTH versions,
     26 microseconds apart, from the same virtual MAC to the same group. The v2
     frame is 20 bytes of VRRP against v3's 12 (v2 carries the 8-byte auth
     field) and expresses the identical 1 s interval as `intvl 1s` instead of
     `intvl 100cs`. swi_b was unaffected and stayed Backup
     [work/s16d-swib-tm-u3.log], as the guide says only the Master needs it.
  ** This is also the cleanest single piece of evidence that the default is v3:
     turning transition mode ON is what makes a v2 advertisement appear. With it
     off, the DUT sends v3 and only v3. **
  Reverted with `disable / transition-mode false / enable` [work/s17-tm-off-u2.log].

